hadiths[46]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2091","Narrated Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There are two blessings which many people do not appreciate: (1) Good health and (2) Free time (i.e., relief from work and moments of leisure)."
"2092","Narrated Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took hold of my shoulder and said: ""Live in this world as if you are a stranger or a wayfarer."" And Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) used to say: ""When you reach the morning, do not expect to reach the evening, and when you reach the evening, do not expect to reach the morning (and do whatever good deeds you can). Perhaps if the morning comes, the evening may not come."" And prepare for illness during your health, and prepare for death during your life."
"2093","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah (bin Mas'ud) رضي الله عنه that the Noble Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم drew a square shape and drew a line extending out from it, and on this line he drew small lines on both sides. He said: ""(Inside the square) is a man, and the square is his death which surrounds him from all sides, and the long line that extends outside the square is man's hope (desire), and these small lines are calamities and accidents (illnesses). If he escapes one calamity, he falls into another, and if he escapes that one, he is afflicted by a third."
"2094","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drew several lines (like the shape in the first hadith) and said: ""This (the line extending out of the circle) is the example of man's desire; he remains engrossed in this desire when death comes to him."
"2095","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever Allah grants a long life until he reaches sixty years, then Allah does not accept his excuse."
"2096","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The heart of an old person remains young in two things: (1) love of the world, (2) and desire for a long life."
"2097","Narrated from Sayyiduna Utban bin Malik Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Whoever says 'La ilaha illallah' purely for the sake of Allah, then on the Day of Resurrection, the fire of Hell will be forbidden for him."
"2098","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says: 'When I take away a beloved thing of a believing servant from the world (such as a son, brother, etc.) and he remains patient over it, then his reward with Me is nothing except Paradise (that is, he will be granted Paradise).'"
"2099","Narrated Sayyiduna Mirdas Aslami (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The righteous people will die first, then those who are less virtuous after them, until only some people will remain like the husk of barley or the refuse of dates, whom Allah does not care about at all."
"2100","Narrated Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""If the son of Adam were to have two valleys full of wealth, he would seek a third, and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust. And Allah turns with mercy to him who turns to Him in repentance."
"2101","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) said that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Who among you is there who loves the wealth of his heir more than his own wealth?"" All of them replied, ""O Messenger of Allah! All of us love our own wealth more."" So he (peace be upon him) said: ""Your own wealth is only that which you spend (in the way of Allah) and send forward during your life, and whatever you leave behind after death, that belongs to your heirs."
"2102","`Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) says:` By Allah, besides Whom there is no deity, sometimes due to hunger I would lie down on the ground with my stomach pressed against it, and sometimes I would tie a stone to my stomach. One day, I sat in the path of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions. First, Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) passed by, so I asked him about a verse of the Qur'an (only) so that he would ask me (about my condition) and take me home and feed me, but he went away. Then Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) passed by, so I said the same to him, but he also went away. Then Abu al-Qasim (Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by. When he saw me, he understood and smiled and said: ""O Abu Hur!"" I said, ""At your service, O Messenger of Allah!"" He said: ""Come with me."" I went along with him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the house, I asked permission to enter, and I was granted permission. I went inside. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a bowl of milk and said: ""Where did this come from?"" The household said, ""So-and-so person,"" or he said, ""So-and-so woman has given it to you as a gift."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O Abu Hur!"" I said, ""At your service, O Messenger of Allah!"" He said: ""Call the people of Suffah."" Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the people of Suffah were guests of the Muslims; they had no home, nor any wealth or possessions, nor any friend or acquaintance whose house they could stay at (they used to stay in the mosque). When any charity would come, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not partake of it himself (because charity was forbidden for him and his family), but would give it to them. And if a gift came, he would keep some for himself and give some to them. Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: ""Go and call the people of Suffah,"" it was very hard on me. I said to myself, ""How will this little milk suffice for the people of Suffah? I was more deserving of this milk; if I drank some, I would gain some strength. And when the people of Suffah come, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) will order me to serve them the milk. When they start drinking, I do not expect that any milk will be left for me at the end. But what could I do? Obeying Allah and His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was absolutely necessary."" So, reluctantly, I went to them and called them. They asked permission to enter, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted them permission. They came and sat in their places. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: ""O Abu Hur!"" I said, ""At your service, O Messenger of Allah!"" He said: ""Serve them this milk."" I began to give the bowl of milk to each one of them. When one finished drinking, he would return the bowl to me. I would give it to the next person, and he too would drink to his fill and return the bowl to me. (Then to the third person, and so on.) In this way, after all of them, the bowl reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). By that time, the people of Suffah had drunk to their fill. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took the bowl in his hand, looked at me, smiled, and said: ""Now only you and I are left."" I said, ""Indeed, O Messenger of Allah!"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Sit down and drink the milk."" I sat down and began to drink the milk. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Drink more."" So I drank more. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept saying this until I said, ""By the One Who sent you with the truth, now there is no more room in my stomach."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Alright, now give it to me."" I gave it to him, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praised Allah, said Bismillah, and drank the remaining milk. (This was also one of the miracles of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him.)"
"2103","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) made this supplication: ""O Allah! Grant sustenance to the family of Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) that is sufficient for their needs."
"2104","Narrated Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""No one will be saved because of his deeds (rather, it will be by Allah's mercy)."" The people asked, ""Not even you, O Messenger of Allah?"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) replied: ""Not even me, unless Allah's mercy envelops me."" And he said: ""Act with moderation, seek closeness to Allah, and worship in the morning, evening, and a part of the night, and acting with moderation will lead you to your desired destination (i.e., Paradise)."
"2105","Narrated from Ummul Momineen Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was asked: Which deed is most beloved to Allah Almighty? He replied: ""That deed which is done consistently, even if it is little."
"2106","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""When Allah created mercy, He created it in one hundred parts. He kept ninety-nine parts with Himself and sent one part to the entire creation. So if the disbelievers knew all the mercy that is with Allah, they would never despair of Paradise (despite their disbelief, polytheism, etc.), and if the believers knew all the punishment that is with Allah, they would never feel safe from Hell (despite their faith, belief, and righteous deeds)."
"2107","Narrated from Sayyiduna Sahl bin Sa'd (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever guarantees me (the proper use of) what is between his jaws and what is between his legs, I guarantee Paradise for him."" (i.e., he never misuses these two in the rights of Allah or the rights of people.)"
"2108","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A person may utter a word that pleases Allah, without giving it any importance, and because of that Allah raises his ranks. And (sometimes) a person may utter a word that angers Allah, and he does not consider it a major sin, yet because of that he falls into Hell."
"2109","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""My example and the example of what Allah has sent me with is like that of a person who came to a people and said: I have seen with my own eyes that an enemy army is coming, and I am clearly warning you to save yourselves from it, save yourselves from it. A group accepted his word and left that place during the night, so they were saved. But another group did not accept his word; in the morning, the army arrived and destroyed them."
"2110","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Hell is veiled with desires, and Paradise is veiled with things that the soul dislikes."
"2111","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Paradise is closer to you than the strap of your sandal, and likewise, Hell is closer to you than the strap of your sandal."" (So be cautious.)"
"2112","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When any one of you looks at someone who is wealthier than him, he should also look at someone who is less fortunate than him."
"2113","Narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said among other Qudsi narrations: “Allah Almighty has written down good deeds and bad deeds and has made it clear which is a good deed and which is a bad deed. So whoever intends to do a good deed but does not do it, Allah will write a complete good deed in his record. And whoever intends to do a good deed and then does it, Allah will write for him ten to seven hundred good deeds, or even more, as much as He wills. And whoever intends to do a bad deed but refrains from doing it (out of fear of Allah), Allah will write a complete good deed for him. And whoever intends to do a bad deed and then does it, only one sin will be written for him.”"
"2114","Sayyiduna Abu Hudhaifah (may Allah be pleased with him) said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated two hadiths to me; I have witnessed the fulfillment of one, and I am awaiting the fulfillment of the other. The first hadith is: ""Trustworthiness was first instilled in the depths of the hearts, then people learned about the command of trustworthiness from the Qur'an, and then they learned it from the Sunnah of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."" And regarding the disappearance of trustworthiness, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Trustworthiness will soon be taken away, and it will happen that a man will sleep and trustworthiness will be removed from his heart. Its effect will remain like a faint mark. Then he will sleep again, and the remaining trustworthiness will also be removed, and its sign will be like a blister, as if you kick a burning coal with your foot and it swells up, and you see it raised, though there is nothing inside it. In the morning, people will get up and engage in buying and selling, but there will not be a trustworthy person among them. Trustworthy people will become so rare that people will say in amazement (that, brother) in such-and-such tribe, such-and-such person is so trustworthy, and about a person they will say how clever, wise, and brave he is, though there will not be even a mustard seed's worth of faith in his heart."" Then he narrates that a time has passed over me when I had no hesitation in dealing with anyone. Islam would bring a Muslim to give me my due, and a Christian's ruler would compel him to give me my right. But nowadays, I do not deal or buy and sell with anyone except so-and-so and so-and-so."
"2115","Narrated Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""The condition of people is like that of camels; out of a hundred camels, you will not find a single camel fit for riding swiftly."
"2116","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Jundub (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever does a good deed to show off to the creation, Allah will make his bad intention known to everyone (on the Day of Resurrection), and whoever does a good deed to be seen by people, Allah will also show his true reality to everyone on the Day of Resurrection."" (And they will not receive any reward.)"
"2117","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says: Whoever shows enmity to My friend, I declare war against him. And nothing is more beloved to Me by which My servant draws near to Me than what I have made obligatory upon him. And My servant continues to draw near to Me through supererogatory acts until I love him. And when I love him, I become his hearing with which he hears, his sight with which he sees, his hand with which he grasps, and his foot with which he walks. And if he asks Me (for anything), I surely grant it to him, and if he seeks refuge with Me, I surely grant him refuge. And I do not hesitate in anything as I hesitate in taking the soul of the believer; he dislikes death and I dislike to displease him."
"2118","It is narrated from Sayyiduna ‘Ubada bin Samit (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Whoever likes to meet Allah, Allah also likes to meet him; and whoever dislikes to meet Allah, Allah also dislikes to meet him.” Umm al-Mu’minin ‘A’ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) or one of the other noble wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) submitted, “We also dislike death.” So the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “That is not (the meaning); rather, the meaning is that when the time of death comes for a believer, he is given the glad tidings of Allah’s pleasure and honor. At that moment, nothing ahead of him (i.e., meeting Allah) seems better to him, so he likes to meet Allah and Allah likes to meet him. And when the time of death comes for a disbeliever, he is informed of Allah’s punishment and torment. So nothing ahead of him (i.e., punishment and torment) seems worse to him, and he dislikes to meet Allah and Allah dislikes to meet him.”"
"2119","Narrated from Ummul Momineen Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that some Bedouins and harsh-natured people from Arabia used to come to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) and ask: ""When will that Hour (the Day of Judgment) come?"" The Prophet (peace be upon him) would look towards the youngest among them and say: ""If this one lives, old age will not come upon him before the Hour comes upon you, meaning you will die (and death is also a kind of Hour)."
"2120","Narrated Abu Sa'id Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""On the Day of Resurrection, the earth will be like a loaf of bread which Allah, the Exalted, will turn over with His Hand, just as one of you turns over his bread during a journey. This will be a feast for the people of Paradise."" (The narrator says) Then a Jew came and said, ""O Abul-Qasim! May Allah bless you, shall I not inform you of the feast of the people of Paradise on the Day of Resurrection?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Yes, tell me."" He said the same as the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had said, that the earth (on the Day of Resurrection) will be like a loaf of bread. (The narrator says that) when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard this, he looked towards us and smiled until his blessed teeth became visible. Then the Jew said, ""Shall I not tell you what its relish will be?"" Its relish will be balam and noon. The Companions (may Allah be pleased with them) asked, ""What are these?"" He said, ""Ox and fish."" These ox and fish will be so large that a piece hanging from their liver will be eaten by seventy thousand people of Paradise."
"2121","Sahih Sahl bin Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: “On the Day of Resurrection, people will be gathered on a land that is pure and white like a loaf of white wheat bread.” Sahl (may Allah be pleased with him) or another narrator says: There will be no mark of any kind on that (land)."
"2122","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): People will be gathered in three ways. One group will be those who will be hopeful and fearful, and (the second group) will be those who will ride two by two, three by three, four by four, and ten by ten on a single camel. And the rest of the people will be gathered by fire; wherever they rest, it will rest as well, and wherever they spend the night, it will spend the night as well, and wherever they reach the morning, it will reach the morning as well, and wherever they reach the evening, it will reach the evening as well. (That is, it will bring them to the field of gathering.)"
"2123","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You will be raised barefoot, naked, and uncircumcised."" So I asked, ""O Messenger of Allah! Will men and women look at each other's (private parts)?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""That time will be so severe that no one will even think of such a thing."
"2124","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""On the Day of Resurrection, people will sweat so much that it will spread over the earth and will go down seventy cubits into the ground (the earth will become wet to that depth), and people will be submerged in their sweat up to their mouths, or half of their ears."
"2125","Sayyiduna Abdullah (bin Mas'ud) (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The first matter that will be decided among the people on the Day of Judgment will be concerning bloodshed."
"2126","Narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the people of Paradise will enter Paradise and the people of Hell will enter Hell, then death will be brought and placed between Paradise and Hell, and then it will be slaughtered. Then a caller will announce: O people of Paradise! (after today) there will be no death for you, and O people of Hell! (after today) there will be no death for you either. (Upon hearing this) the people of Paradise will rejoice even more, and the people of Hell will be grieved even more."
"2127","Narrated from Abu Sa'id Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah, the Exalted, will say to the people of Paradise: O people of Paradise! They will say: O our Lord! We are present and ready for every command. Allah, the Exalted, will say: Are you pleased? They will say: How could we not be pleased when You have granted us such blessings that You have not granted to any of Your creation? Allah, the Exalted, will say: I will bestow upon you something even greater than that. The people of Paradise will say: O our Lord! What is that thing which is better than this? Allah, the Exalted, will say: I bestow My pleasure upon you, and I will never be displeased with you again."
"2128","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""(On the Day of Resurrection, in Hell) the distance between the two shoulders (shoulder blades) of a disbeliever will be equal to the distance a fast rider covers in three days."
"2129","Narrated by Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: ""Some people (due to their evil deeds) will come out of Hell after being punished and will enter Paradise, so the people of Paradise will call them 'the people of Hell.'"
"2130","Narrated by Sayyiduna Nu'man bin Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him): I heard the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""On the Day of Resurrection, the person with the lightest punishment will be the one under whose feet two embers will be placed, and because of them his brain will boil just as a pot boils."
"2131","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""No person enters Paradise except that his place in Hell, if he had done evil deeds, will be shown to him so that he may be more grateful; and no person enters Hell except that his house in Paradise, if he had done good deeds, will be shown to him so that he may feel more regret."
"2132","`Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with both of them) narrates:` The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""My reservoir (Kawthar, in its length and width) is the distance of a month's journey. Its water is whiter than milk and more fragrant than musk, and its drinking vessels (cups, goblets, etc.) are like the stars in the sky. Whoever drinks from it (even once) will never feel thirsty again."
"2133","Narrated by Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""My reservoir (Kawthar) will be before you. Its size is as great as the distance from Jurba to Azrah."
"2134","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The size of my cistern is as much as the distance from Aylah to Sana'a (and both these cities are located in the land of Yemen), and its drinking vessels are as numerous as the stars in the sky."
"2135","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On the Day of Resurrection, I will be standing at the Hawd (the Pond). A group will come, and when I recognize them, a person (an angel) will come out between me and them and say (to those people), 'Go.' I will say, 'Where are you taking them?' He will say, 'To the Fire, by Allah (where else).' I will say, 'What is the reason for this?' He will say, 'These people turned back on their heels (abandoned the religion) after your death (and put Allah's commands behind their backs).' Then (after them) another group will come, and when I recognize them (that they are from my Ummah), a person (an angel) will come out between me and them and say, 'Go.' I will say, 'Where will you take them?' He will say, 'To the Fire.' I will say, 'Why?' He will say, 'These people turned back on their heels after your death.' (And put Allah's commands behind their backs.) The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'Then only a very few of them will be saved.'"
"2136","Narrated Haritha bin Wahb (may Allah be pleased with him): I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) mention the Hawd (Pond) of Kawthar, and he said: ""Its length is like the distance from Madinah to Sana'a in Yemen."
